Start();
register(OwnTermT);
define
    otSep=";";
    otDelim=[;];
    otSrc=(a;b;c;d#);
    otHits=0;
    otField isRule otCell=otDelim{ otSep? guard='n' code={
        otSeen := otSep.isGrouP;
        if *otSeen == 1;     ++otHits;
        return otCell;
        };
    otRun code={
        pushInputField(argument);
        otField();
        otField();
        otField();
        popInputField();
        otG := otSep.isGrouP;
        otD := otSep.datA;
        cerr "OT global isGroup " otG " data " otD " hits " otHits " text [" otSep "]":;
        };
    ;
otRun(otSrc);
cerr "OWNTERMLOCALT SENTINEL":;
stop();

A rule's body names one of the rule's own terms (otSep), and a global of that name exists and is what the term matches
with. The body's name must be a local that takes the label, never the global (Tony, 2026-11-24;
ruleActions.rtn resolveName, ownTermIsLocal). Before the change the label bind wrote the label into the global, so the
term stopped matching on the second call and the global was emptied on the third.

The row wants: the global still a string after three fires (isGroup 0, data 13, text ;), and hits 3. Hits is the
non-zero sibling: it counts the fires in which the body saw the label under the term's name, so it is 3 only when the
term matched all three times. Before the change the line read isGroup 0 data 0 hits 1 text [otSep].
